WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You look great.
You look like a million bucks.

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don't look tired, and
I would have thought you did,

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:05.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you went on a
vacation with your family.

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:06.373 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes. Yes, I did.

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:08.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you have
a couple of older kids

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:10.076 line:92%
and you've got a 10-month-old.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:10.610 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I do, yes.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:11.911
-And you took your 10-month-old
to the Bahamas.

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:14.080 size:84% position:42%
How was your first trip
with a 10-month-old?

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what? It was great.
-Okay, good.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I got a good 10-month-old.
-Yeah.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:20.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's, like, a 10-month-old,
but he's like 30.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:24.057
-Oh, that's good.
-Yeah, he's very, very relaxed.

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:27.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, he's extremely mature.
He can chill.

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:28.928 size:78% position:39% line:92%
He can just watch TV.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:32.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he'll change and
just look at you for a while.

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:34.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's sometimes where you
got to pluck him,

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.302 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
make sure he alive.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:36.870 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, right.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's the one downside of
a chill baby, yeah.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Hey, man,
are you breathing, man?"

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
He'll just sit with
his mouth open.

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:44.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he's amazing, man.
I love him.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.779
-Here you are with your family,
and I want to --

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:47.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
First of all,
I should note you went --

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:49.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a pig --
A beach that has pigs on it.

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:50.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh yeah, yeah, yeah.
Pig island.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Pig island.
-Pig island, yes.

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:53.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, there you are
with some pigs, but --

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:56.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's fascinating,
but what's more fascinating --

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:57.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
is it fair to say
that your entire family

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
is wearing the same
patterned swimsuit?

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:00.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
-100%. 100%.
-Okay.

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:03.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
Gotcha. And was that
an accident or on purpose?

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:06.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, it's because I'm black.
That's what we do.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:09.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
Black people --
we like to match.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:13.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a thing.
We go overboard with matching.

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:15.008 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I am that dad.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations on
"Night School."

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:17.811 line:92%
This is a really funny film.

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:20.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is based,
on some degree,

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.514 line:92%
on your own experiences, yeah?

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:23.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, 100%.
It's based on second chances.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's what the whole purpose
behind the movie is.

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:30.023
You know, I think so many people
frown on second chances.

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:32.692
You know, when you don't get
something right the first time,

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:33.760 size:84% position:42% line:92%
ultimately, you're down

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you feel like,
"I'm not going to do it.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going to go
in another direction.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:37.864 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's over."

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:40.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, this is a movie
that shows that it's okay

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
to go back the second time
and give it your all

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:45.171
and take the things that you
didn't do right the first time,

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
apply it to that second time,
and come out better.

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:50.043
And, sometimes, it takes a third
and fourth time, you know?

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:53.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's what this is about.

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:55.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I'm a victim
of not getting it right

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:56.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
the first time
for a lot of things.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:02:00.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You've got a great cast --
Tiffany Haddish, Taran Killam.

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:00.620 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.056
-You also -- I know, in the prep
for this, you got to --

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:04.691 size:75% position:38%
You were a principal
for a day in Dallas.

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:05.258 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, I was. Yes.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:09.295
-You gave sort of a TED Talk
of sorts to kids in Atlanta.

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:10.130 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:12.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What do you try to
impart upon students?

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:13.433 line:92%
-Well, the first thing is rules.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:15.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, when I got to be
principal for a day,

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:18.304
I felt it was very important to
make my presence felt.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:21.774
You know, I'm a big fan of
Joe Clark on "Lean On Me."

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:22.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:25.078
-Yeah, yeah. That's right.
Those are the people that know.

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:27.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Some Joe Clark fans.
-That's right -- Joe Clark.

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:28.214 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He's the real deal.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:31.718
"You smoke crack, don't you?"
That's one of the best lines.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:34.587
But I said, you know,
I wanted to change some things.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:35.622 line:92%
So the first thing I did was --

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:38.424
I said, "We're going to
have chicken nuggets every day."

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:39.092 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, that's good.

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:40.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
No one's going to fight
you on that.

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:41.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I like nuggets.
That was a great rule.

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:45.398
I took all the
toilet paper out the bathrooms,

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:46.232 line:92%
replaced it with baby wipes,

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:50.837
and said, "It's important that
we all wipe our asses properly."

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:51.371 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:52.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You now,
that's something I did.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:54.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Especially after, like,
nuggets every day.

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:55.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, after nuggets,
you're going to need it.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:57.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, yeah, yeah. You get it.
You get where I'm going.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.678 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:01.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I was on a roll, and
then the real principal came,

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:03.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he was like,
"This has to stop."

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:05.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-He took my bullhorn away.

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:08.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I gave,
actually, a real speech

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:08.922 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and I told the kids --

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:10.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "It's very important
to embrace this moment

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:12.659 size:78% position:39%
and really understand
what teachers are."

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:15.995
I now, at the age of 39,
understand the importance

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.697 line:92%
and value behind these teachers.

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:20.366 size:81% position:41%
You know, teachers are
investing time, energy

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.468 size:84% position:42%
into these kids because
they feel like the kids

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:25.371
are our next generation's
leaders and groundbreakers.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:28.441
And I said,
"Your biggest reward to them is

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
by doing something
with your life.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:33.646
Take advantage of this time
and really apply yourself."

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:36.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
And, you know, it was good.

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:38.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was good because
they related, they responded.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.453 size:75% position:38%
They identified with
what I was saying,

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:41.521 line:92%
because it was coming from me.

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a fantastic message
to give them.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:46.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also -- Another
thing that's interesting is --

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:48.595
you know, I think people look at
you and they think, "Oh, my God.

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:49.529 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You're so successful."

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:50.730 line:92%
Everything you do is successful,

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:55.568
but you have also had films
that did not particularly work.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:57.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were in a film,
"Soul Plane."

00:03:57.637 --> 00:04:02.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Soul Plane" was not
a huge box-office success.

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:02.575 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:06.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you have a theory
as to what went wrong here,

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:07.947 line:92%
and your theory is based on --

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:08.815 line:92%
-Well, it got bootlegged.

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:11.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
My movie was bootlegged
before it came out.

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you know the background
of "Soul Plane"?

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:16.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know.
-Oh, let me educate you.

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:17.490 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So, "Soul Plane"...

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Soul Plane" was supposed
to be the one.

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was going to
take me out of here.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Oh, my God.

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:24.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's about to go down, okay?
-Uh-huh.

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:25.732 line:92%
-This is -- Here it comes.

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:27.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
Somebody give me
the money train,

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause after this movie,
it's going to happen.

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:31.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-I'm at the airport.

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're still
filming the movie, actually.

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:36.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're doing reshoots.
And a guy comes up to me.

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:37.710 size:84% position:42% line:92%
He's like, "Oh, my God.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're the guy from
'Soul Plane.'"

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:41.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like,
"Hey, how you doing, man?"

00:04:41.014 --> 00:04:42.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like,
"Man, the movie's funny."

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:44.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Well, you're going to

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
really think
it's funny when it come out."

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:48.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like, "No, it's out.
I saw it."

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:50.323 line:92%
And I was like, "No, you didn't.

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:52.792
You couldn't have seen it,
because we're still shooting it.

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:54.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're actually shooting
it right now."

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:55.728 line:92%
He was like, "No, I saw it.

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:57.563
I could tell you everything that
happened in the movie."

00:04:57.563 --> 00:05:00.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he starts telling me all
the scenes in the movie.

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:03.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was like, "Dude, would you
mind signing it for me?"

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:04.737 line:92%
And I said, "Signing what?"

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:09.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he pulls
the bootleg out of his bag

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:10.810 line:92%
and he's like, "Sign it."

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:11.744 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And I had no choice.

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:13.880
I had to sign it,
'cause it's the first autograph

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:14.981 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I've ever really given.

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:16.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So I was excited.

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:18.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I immediately,
like, called the director

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:19.585 line:92%
and I was like, "Hey, man,

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:22.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
a guy just told me
he had the bootleg."

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:23.089 line:92%
And he's like, "No. No way."

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:25.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
Before we knew it,
in like a month,

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:27.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was the biggest thing
on the streets.

00:05:27.427 --> 00:05:30.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody had this movie,
and the movie --

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.066 size:78% position:39%
the date that it was
supposed to come out,

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:34.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
we had to push it up
like a month

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they was like,
"We got to just get it out."

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:38.504 line:92%
So we were trying to lie.

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:39.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were like,
"There's new scenes

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:41.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you haven't seen
in the bootleg."

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:44.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's was like,
"Oh, you think you've seen it.

00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:47.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, wait till
you see the new stuff."

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So your release
was effectively like,

00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:52.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We're re-releasing
'Soul Plane.'

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:56.823
-We had to re-release based off
the bootleg.

00:05:56.823 --> 00:06:00.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were like, "We know
you think you know the end,

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.295 line:92%
but look at what we just added."

00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:05.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we're, like,
cutting together trailers

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:07.166 line:92%
that aren't even in the movie.

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:10.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's, like, me fighting
somebody in karate,

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.404 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
like, "Aah, aah!"

00:06:11.404 --> 00:06:12.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was like,
"Wait till you see this

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:15.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
new action scene in
'Soul Plane.'"

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:18.811
And the movie ended up being
the biggest hit on the streets

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:20.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
but one of the biggest flops
in the box office.

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:23.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
But there is a positive
in every negative.

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:24.617 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
The positive is --

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:28.187
that's how the following
for me in comedy started.

00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:29.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was able to
go to comedy clubs,

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:31.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they were like,
"That's the guy."

00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:32.425 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:06:32.425 --> 00:06:35.395
-I was, "That's the guy from
'Soul Plane'" for a long time.

00:06:35.395 --> 00:06:37.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, thanks so much
for being here.

